    "body": "The fourth lab asked on #1401 for the native Lorentz read's run packet, so the next decision can reuse the existing work rather than launch a duplicate training campaign. References #820.\n\n## What is included\n\nThe packet is `docs/evidence/native-lorentz-packet-2026-09-26/`, 104 files and 4.3 MB.\n\n- **Reports:** every run report.\n  - the 600-step pilot, including the scratch Euclidean and flat-Dot arms;\n  - the context-128 comparison (4 code seeds, 1 WikiText);\n  - the context-256 runs and their probe analyses;\n  - functional checks;\n  - post-training and quantization-aware integer parity, fine-tunes, and idle timing.\n- **Sources:**\n  - the scratch harnesses;\n  - the byte-level BPE tokenizer (`bpe.rs`);\n  - the corpus builder (`make_code_data.py`);\n  - launchers and analysis scripts;\n  - the ablation copy of the training crate as `euclidean-control.patch` against `9df1afab`. It carries the `dotflat` and `euclid` control arms, and the README records their launch lines.\n- **Packed models:** the four quantization-aware integer models and the sealed table root, with the arcosh table. All four load from the packet with `IntegerModel::load_with_tables`, which was checked.\n- **`manifest.json`:** SHA-256 and size for every packet file, and for 136 binaries (465 MB) kept outside the repository. These are the float models, checkpoints, both corpora, probe dumps and harness binaries.\n- The cycle-3 note links the packet.\n\n## Scope kept explicit (README)\n\n- The flat-Dot equal-start control was not run at context 256, and Dot seed 2 is read-dependent.\n- The Euclidean control ran only in the 600-step pilot, with one seed and a sharp start.\n- Integer parity: NLL agrees within 0.0001 nats, but the largest single deviation exceeds the 0.01 limit over 131,072 positions, for both geometries.\n- The Lorentz read's two learned signed16 scalars and derived Q32 scale sit beside the ≤4-bit weight maps. Their D10 status awaits the owner.\n- The corpus split hashes absolute paths, so rebuilding is not bit-exact elsewhere; the hashes pin its identity. The scratch tokenizer is independent of `DialogueProtocol`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- The four packed models load from the packet path, checked through `uor-r4-integer pack-development`.\n- `python3 scripts/check_claim_wording.py`: passed.\n- Docs and evidence only, so no Rust changes.\n\n## Open item\n\nThe 465 MB of binaries outside the packet live in the lab session's scratch, which is not durable. A durable copy needs the owner's choice: an evidence branch, the SSD, or selected files in the repository.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_018jzJYgXbX8FmctqekthjLJ\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_018jzJYgXbX8FmctqekthjLJ)_",
